# Esc while a reply is busy in flight (held back by delay, before any
# text has streamed in yet): the router's Interrupt action aborts the
# turn and commits the "Interrupted" note.
@faux testdata/faux/qa/errors-esc-stream.yaml

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
SHOT welcome
TYPE tell me something slowly
KEY enter
WAIT 1
SHOT mid-flight-before-esc
KEY esc
# design: Terminal.dc.html:312
WAITFOR /Interrupted\. Tell kiln what to do instead\./ 20
SHOT interrupted
EXPECT /■ Interrupted\. Tell kiln what to do instead\./
EXPECT_NOT /This reply is held back long enough/
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
